<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Weak demand weighs on basis.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Weak demand weighs on basis.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were weaker at several locations Thursday, depressed by sluggish domestic and export demand, grain merchandisers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The basis popped (fell) yesterday at both Kansas City and the (U.S.) Gulf so it looks like there is no domestic or export demand,&quot; one Kansas-based merchandiser said.</p>
<p>The basis at Galveston, Texas was down five cents at 60 cents over May KCBT futures and has now fallen eight cents in two days.  </p>
